## System Architecture

The system follows a Dual-Stream Engine architecture.

```text
                  Camera Input
                        |
          +-------------+-------------+
          |                           |
          v                           v

   Stream A                     Stream B
 (Semantic AI)              (Geometric CV)

 Style Transfer          Optical Flow
 Texture Mapping         Edge Detection
 Color Mood              Saliency Analysis

          +-------------+-------------+
                        |
                        v
               Tensor Fusion Layer
                        |
                        v
             Vector Rendering Engine
                        |
                        v
                 Artistic Output
```

---

## Stream A: Semantic Processing

### Purpose
Defines the artistic appearance of the scene.

### Inputs
- RGB video frames
- Downscaled resolution (320×240)

### Operations
- Neural Style Transfer
- Texture generation
- Color palette extraction

### Technologies
- ONNX Runtime
- Quantized INT8 Models
- Feed-Forward Style Networks

### Output
A stylized texture map used by the rendering engine.

---

## Stream B: Geometric Processing

### Purpose
Captures motion and scene structure.

### Inputs
- Current frame
- Previous frame

### Operations
- Dense Optical Flow
- Sobel Edge Detection
- Saliency Segmentation

### Output
A geometric control matrix containing:

- Motion vectors
- Edge directions
- Saliency masks

---

## Tensor Fusion Layer

The rendering engine combines outputs from both streams.

Each virtual brushstroke is represented as:

```math
S = {x, y, l, θ, c, v}
```

Where:

| Symbol | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| x,y | Stroke position |
| l | Stroke length |
| θ | Stroke orientation |
| c | RGB color |
| v | Motion velocity |

The resulting brushstrokes are dynamically updated and rendered onto the digital canvas.

