---

### 2. Dense Optical Flow

Used to simulate wet paint motion.

#### Particle Update Equation

```math
x(t+1) = x(t) + αu
y(t+1) = y(t) + αv
```

Where:

- α = fluid viscosity coefficient
- u,v = optical flow velocity

#### Algorithm

- Farneback Dense Optical Flow
- Motion vector estimation
- Paint advection simulation

---

### 3. Saliency-Based Brush Assignment

Foreground objects receive finer detail than the background.

#### Rule

```text
If M(x,y) >= threshold:
    Fine Brush
Else:
    Coarse Brush
```

#### Benefits

- Better visual quality
- Reduced computational cost
- Improved rendering efficiency

---

### 4. Edge-Aware Stroke Orientation

Brushes align with scene contours.

#### Sobel Gradient Computation

```math
G = √(Gx² + Gy²)
```

```math
ϕ = atan2(Gy, Gx)
```

Stroke orientation:

```math
θ = ϕ + π/2
```

This ensures strokes follow object boundaries naturally.

